meta:
  origin:
    # Data product / Snapshot
    title: Federico-Tena World Trade Historical Database
    description: |-
      The Federico-Tena World Trade Historical Database reports series of imports and exports at current and constant prices, and at current and constant (1913) borders, for almost all polities from 1800 to 1938. Federico and Tena-Junguito (2019) describe the database and its estimation methodology, and build from it an index of world trade volume by summing exports at constant prices.
    # NOTE: The file was received by email and is a later revision of the database's public release (October
    # 2017, https://doi.org/10.21950/JKZFDP): the world trade index matches it exactly up to 1884 and within 1.2%
    # for 1885–1938. Its 1950 value links the series to United Nations trade statistics; there is no 1939–1949.
    date_published: "2019-03-15"

    # Citation
    producer: Federico and Tena-Junguito
    citation_full: |-
      Federico, G., & Tena-Junguito, A. (2019). World trade, 1800-1938: A new synthesis. Revista de Historia Económica / Journal of Iberian and Latin American Economic History, 37(1), 9–41. https://doi.org/10.1017/S0212610918000216

    # Files
    url_main: https://doi.org/10.1017/S0212610918000216
    date_accessed: '2025-09-22'

    # License
    license:
      name: CC BY 4.0
      url: https://edatos.consorciomadrono.es/dataset.xhtml?persistentId=doi:10.21950/JKZFDP
